# Files kept OUT of the published pub.dev package (gitignore-style).
#
# ⚠ When a .pubignore exists, `pub publish` uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore (they
# do NOT combine). So the build-artifact excludes .gitignore provides must be
# repeated here — otherwise publishing from a tree that has been built/tested
# bloats the package with caches (a stray build/ added ~43 MB in dry-run).
#
# Mirrors the public-mirror denylist: internal planning / agent
# / session docs must never reach consumers.

# Build artifacts & caches (re-stated from .gitignore, see note above)
build/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
coverage/
*.log

# Agent + planning docs
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
REFACTOR_PLAN.md
PARITY_MATRIX.md
PARITY_VERIFICATION_*.md
HANDOFF_*.md
doc/superpowers/

# Session state
SESSION_STATE.md

# Internal-only surfaces — keep the consumable package to the showcase, not the
# QA tooling or the tests.
#
# Scoped to `debug/internal/`, NOT to `debug/`: the recorder (`debug_log.dart`)
# and the Debug tab (`debug_tab.dart`) are public surfaces of the showcase —
# `lib/main.dart` and the Events Log scenario import them, so excluding them
# ships an example that cannot compile. Only the Settings debug-console sheet
# and the QA entrypoint are internal.
example/lib/debug/internal/
test/

# Internal dev / release scripts — none of these belong in the consumed
# package. Mirrors `.gitattributes` (`scripts export-ignore`) and the
# public-mirror allowlist, which both keep scripts/ out of the public
# distribution (e.g. run-sample.sh references the demo backend and dev
# tooling). .pubignore governs the pub.dev tarball independently of those,
# so it must repeat the exclusion — otherwise the launcher ships to pub.dev.
scripts/

# Opt-in local git hooks — dev-only, not consumed by host apps.
lefthook.yml

# Release tooling — not part of the consumable package
melos.yaml
